From a3ce67fa0245f06358dbdc9d5564bc04f6604ee4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:14:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] Bugfix: base the vertex label arrays gathered by
 distributed ordering writers [report R. Perry]

`dorderSaveTree2()` gathered the vertex labels of all processes into
an un-based array, using the based process displacement array, so that
the root process wrote `baseval` cells past the end of the array, and
the tree and mapping writers, which index the array with based vertex
numbers, read past its end. Base the label array before gathering, as
`dorderSave()` and `dmapSave()` now do.

In `dorderSave()`, the label array pointer was not initialized on
non-root processes, which nonetheless offset it by the base value.
Set it to NULL and base it on the root process only.

Add a based, labeled graph to the `dgord` checks, with tree output.

Refs: DMO-02
